unit: manage a systemd unit file

A change of the file, also of its owner or mode, runs systemctl
daemon-reload. It does not restart a running unit; a handler with
restarted: true does.

Keys:
  name     string  required  The unit file name with its type, such as app.service or app@.service.
  source   string  -         A file in the recipe's files directory.
  content  string  -         The content of the unit file.

Example:
  - unit:
      name: app.service
      content: |
        [Unit]
        Description=App

        [Service]
        ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/app

        [Install]
        WantedBy=multi-user.target

Run "winch doc unit.<key>" for the full text of a key.
